From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] s: pass the modular USB controller path to Poseidon

The ARM package can register usb2otg.device by basename because the device is
already resident.  Bellatrix deliberately keeps the controller replaceable on
disk under DEVS:USBHardware, so OpenDevice cannot find it by that basename.

Pass the path that exists on disk.  Poseidon's device task first tries the full
name and retains its existing fallback through path components.
---
 workbench/s/Startup-Sequence | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence b/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
+++ b/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ EndIf
 ; that is actually present, if one is.
 If EXISTS "DEVS:USBHardware/usb2otg.device"
     Echo "starting AddUSBHardware" >"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
-    AddUSBHardware usb2otg.device >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+    AddUSBHardware DEVS:USBHardware/usb2otg.device >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
     Echo "finished AddUSBHardware" >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
 EndIf
 Run <NIL: >NIL: QUIET ConClip
